<gpx version="1.1" creator="galicica.finereli.com" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:gpxx="http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/GpxExtensions/v3" xmlns:gpx_style="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/gpx_style/0/2">
<metadata><name>Elshani - Bugarska Chuka - Lako Signoj - Galičica pass</name><desc>Mostly a ridge walk, and mostly on soft ground that's pleasant underfoot, except from Elshani up to Bugarska Chuka, where it's hard and stony. Apart from short stretches above Elshani there's no vegetation along the path. For most of the way the trail is clear and, in good visibility, easy to follow. Along the way are many historic sites, mostly from the First World War. The park calls it one of the most attractive trails in Macedonia, for the sense of space and the views. https://galicica.finereli.com/routes/elshani-bugarska-chuka-lako-signoj-galicica-pass/</desc><link href="https://galicica.finereli.com/"><text>galicica.finereli.com</text></link><copyright author="NP Galičica (trail lines), OpenStreetMap contributors (places, G-6)"><license>https://galicica.finereli.com/about/#license</license></copyright></metadata>
<wpt lat="41.026367" lon="20.817080"><name>Start: Galičica pass (regional road R-504)</name><desc>Galičica pass (regional road R-504) to Elshani village: 13.3 km, 5 h 30 min, moderate</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="40.954004" lon="20.829229"><name>Start: Elshani village</name><desc>Elshani village to Galičica pass (regional road R-504): 13.3 km, 6 h 30 min, hard</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<trk><name>T-5: Elshani to the G-5 junction</name><desc>T-5 is one of Galičica National Park's harder and longer hiking trails, with more climbing. It's 3.7 km from Elshani to the G-5 junction, with about 654 m of climbing and 0 m of descent in the direction drawn, between 887 m and 1,547 m.</desc><type>T</type><extensions><gpxx:TrackExtension><gpxx:DisplayColor>DarkGreen</gpxx:DisplayColor></gpxx:TrackExtension><gpx_style:line><gpx_style:color>1F7A3D</gpx_style:color><gpx_style:width>4</gpx_style:width></gpx_style:line></extensions><trkseg><trkpt lat="41.026367" lon="20.817080"><ele>887</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026809" lon="20.817757"><ele>898</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026938" lon="20.818278"><ele>907</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027017" lon="20.818909"><ele>916</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026984" lon="20.819101"><ele>920</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027252" lon="20.819671"><ele>933</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027210" lon="20.819813"><ele>937</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027101" lon="20.819845"><ele>939</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026946" lon="20.819746"><ele>937</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026878" lon="20.819835"><ele>943</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026797" lon="20.819913"><ele>949</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026764" lon="20.819891"><ele>950</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026665" lon="20.819875"><ele>952</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026620" lon="20.820000"><ele>955</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026712" lon="20.820255"><ele>961</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026714" lon="20.820268"><ele>961</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026694" lon="20.820270"><ele>962</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026824" lon="20.820608"><ele>969</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026839" lon="20.820622"><ele>969</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026861" lon="20.820597"><ele>969</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.026995" lon="20.820678"><ele>973</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027010" lon="20.821002"><ele>984</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027063" lon="20.820914"><ele>980</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="41.027101" lon="20.821112"><ele>987</e